  ('11a19d18-3b98-4b6a-b310-9ab4aba1f7c8', 5,
   $r4$Yea on HB 1296 (2022), conference report (the enrolled text): it repeals the licence to carry ("section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)") and sets who may not carry on permit-free carry ("the following persons may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun"), which is part of the rung 5 act. That meets "Repeal laws that require a permit" … "such as the permit to carry". His Yeas on HB 1071 (2017) and SB 43 (2017) are rung 4 acts on the same side, so the furthest act is 5. His Nay on HB 1365 (2023) is a No vote and shows nothing on a rung. Other ungated votes (HB 1143, a related bill, HB 1274, HB 1323 and SB 176 where present) are adjacent: police-agency disposal, suits against gun makers, insurance notices, licence-record privacy and shooting-range zoning. Gated votes (near-unanimous or multi-subject) cannot seat.$r4$,
