  ('17589403-085b-47af-8f83-7a7cdc3888b0', 4,
   $r4$As State Representative he co-sponsored and voted Yea on MI HB 4980 (2026-01-21, 60-45, gate none), which lets a CPL applicant apply to a county clerk in any county in this state, and HB 4855 (2026-02-05, 90-13), allowing "carrying a loaded pistol, whether concealed or not" while "hunting game with a bow and arrow"; he voted Yea on HB 4284 (CPL renewal fee "$115.00" to "$30.00") and HB 5113 (reapply "without paying an additional fee"). Each keeps the permit and makes carrying easier: 'Make carrying a gun easier, such as honoring carry permits from other states' (rung 4; annex rule two). His own words on HB 4586 (lowering the concealed-carry licence age to 18, 'Every safeguard that exists in our current concealed carry process remains fully intact') describe a lower licence age that keeps the permit, which is direction-only under Q4, and HB 4586 has no instrument file. No act repeals a permit and none is a rung 1-3 act. HB 4481 is gated; HB 4949 is adjacent.$r4$,
   $r4$As State Representative he co-sponsored and voted Yea on MI HB 4980 (2026-01-21, 60-45, gate none), which lets a CPL applicant apply to a county clerk in any county in this state, and HB 4855 (2026-02-05, 90-13), allowing "carrying a loaded pistol, whether concealed or not" while "hunting game with a bow and arrow"; he voted Yea on HB 4284 (CPL renewal fee "$115.00" to "$30.00") and HB 5113 (reapply "without paying an additional fee"). HB 4284 keeps the permit and makes it easier to get: 'Make carrying a gun easier, such as honoring carry permits from other states' (rung 4; annex rule two). Since the 2026-11-12 ruling HB 4980, HB 4855 and HB 5113 show only which side he is on and are not rung acts. His own words on HB 4586 (lowering the concealed-carry licence age to 18, 'Every safeguard that exists in our current concealed carry process remains fully intact') describe a lower licence age that keeps the permit, which is direction-only under Q4, and HB 4586 has no instrument file. No act repeals a permit and none is a rung 1-3 act. HB 4481 is gated; HB 4949 is adjacent.$r4$),
  ('1bc51f76-9feb-4c23-9ee9-1293420c94f0', 3,
   $r4$At the press conference unveiling her bills to ban home-made guns with no serial numbers (Michigan Public, 2025-06-04, in-term), she said: 'No one needs an untraceable ghost gun. These weapons are designed to avoid detection, responsibility, and justice. These are tools for people who intend to do harm and get away with it.' Said to launch a ban on untraceable guns, this backs a ban on having unserialised guns, a rung 3 act under annex rule one: 'Add limits on buying, having or carrying a gun' (serial numbers required, unserialised guns banned). Her Yea on HB 4855 (bow hunters may carry a pistol, rung 4) keeps the permit and, under the licence rule, does not conflict with a serial-number rule, so the record sits at rung 3. Her Nays on HB 4284, HB 4980 and HB 5113 show a side only; her bill numbers have no instrument file and are not cited as records.$r4$,
   $r4$At the press conference unveiling her bills to ban home-made guns with no serial numbers (Michigan Public, 2025-06-04, in-term), she said: 'No one needs an untraceable ghost gun. These weapons are designed to avoid detection, responsibility, and justice. These are tools for people who intend to do harm and get away with it.' Said to launch a ban on untraceable guns, this backs a ban on having unserialised guns, a rung 3 act under annex rule one: 'Add limits on buying, having or carrying a gun' (serial numbers required, unserialised guns banned). Her Yea on HB 4855 (bow hunters may carry a pistol) keeps the permit and since the 2026-11-12 ruling shows only which side she is on. It is not a rung act and conflicts with nothing, so the record sits at rung 3 on her own words. Her Nays on HB 4284, HB 4980 and HB 5113 show a side only; her bill numbers have no instrument file and are not cited as records.$r4$),
  ('1e239b16-89e0-4a93-9724-0df547e079f3', 5,
   $r4$Yea on HB 1296 (2022), conference report (the enrolled text): it repeals the licence to carry ("section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)") and sets who may not carry on permit-free carry ("the following persons may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun"), which is part of the rung 5 act. That meets "Repeal laws that require a permit" … "such as the permit to carry". His Yea on HB 1084 (2024) is a rung 4 act on the same side, so the furthest act is 5. The Yea on HB 1365 (2023) is not read as a rung act: its stored text restates the under-18 machine-gun transfer ban already enacted by SB 119 (2019) and amends the machine-gun definition and its exemption list with no deletion markup, so whether it widens or narrows the ban cannot be read; it neither seats nor makes the record two-sided. Other ungated votes (HB 1143, HB 1235, HB 1274, HB 1323 and SB 176 where present) are adjacent: police-agency disposal, suits against gun makers, insurance notices, licence-record privacy and shooting-range zoning. Gated votes (near-unanimous or multi-subject) cannot seat.$r4$,
   $r4$Yea on HB 1296 (2022), conference report (the enrolled text): it repeals the licence to carry ("section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)") and sets who may not carry on permit-free carry ("the following persons may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun"), which is part of the rung 5 act. That meets "Repeal laws that require a permit" … "such as the permit to carry". His Yea on HB 1084 (2024), a capitol carry right for state officials, is out of scope since the 2026-11-12 ruling (not a rung act). The furthest act is 5. The Yea on HB 1365 (2023) is not read as a rung act: its stored text restates the under-18 machine-gun transfer ban already enacted by SB 119 (2019) and amends the machine-gun definition and its exemption list with no deletion markup, so whether it widens or narrows the ban cannot be read; it neither seats nor makes the record two-sided. Other ungated votes (HB 1143, HB 1235, HB 1274, HB 1323 and SB 176 where present) are adjacent: police-agency disposal, suits against gun makers, insurance notices, licence-record privacy and shooting-range zoning. Gated votes (near-unanimous or multi-subject) cannot seat.$r4$),
  ('1ea3c520-481e-4975-9fcb-ef1c508d680f', 5,
   $r4$Yea on the final Senate vote (conference report, 30-20) for HB 1296 (2022), whose operative text repeals the licence to carry a handgun (the offence of "carrying a handgun without a license" is listed "(before its repeal)") and replaces it with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun" (part of the rung 5 act, closure C3), single-subject,. That meets rung 5, repeal laws that require a permit to carry. His Yea on HB 1084 (2024): "A state officer who is not prohibited from possessing a handgun under state or federal law has the right to carry a handgun within the state capitol building" (carry allowed in a public building where it was barred, rung 4; the registry and payment-code sections are not rung acts) is on the same side. No ungated restriction-side rung act: his HB 1177 (2023) authorship is a multi-subject school-safety bill, and the NRA-membership lines are third-person profile text, not own words.$r4$,
   $r4$Yea on the final Senate vote (conference report, 30-20) for HB 1296 (2022), whose operative text repeals the licence to carry a handgun (the offence of "carrying a handgun without a license" is listed "(before its repeal)") and replaces it with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun" (part of the rung 5 act, closure C3), single-subject,. That meets rung 5, repeal laws that require a permit to carry. His Yea on HB 1084 (2024): "A state officer who is not prohibited from possessing a handgun under state or federal law has the right to carry a handgun within the state capitol building" (a capitol carry right for state officials, which since the 2026-11-12 ruling is out of scope, not a rung act; the registry and payment-code sections are not rung acts) does not change the seat. No ungated restriction-side rung act: his HB 1177 (2023) authorship is a multi-subject school-safety bill, and the NRA-membership lines are third-person profile text, not own words.$r4$),
  ('217b8c85-424b-41df-aa1b-7818425623d7', 5,
   $r4$Yea in the House on the HB 1296 (2022) conference committee report (the rung 5 act, runner ruling): Sec. 10 repeals the licence requirement "Section 1 of this chapter does not apply to" and Sec. 9 replaces it with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun", so an adult not on that list may carry a handgun with no licence. That is a law that repeals the permit to carry (rung 5: "Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry"). Single-subject (season 3 verdict), ungated. His Yea on HB 1084 (2024) (rung 4) sits below it. His 2022 press-release words on a related bill (permitless carry) agree but are out of the current cycle and not relied on; the HB 1296 co-sponsorship is evidence of the bill as filed and is not cited.$r4$,
   $r4$Yea in the House on the HB 1296 (2022) conference committee report (the rung 5 act, runner ruling): Sec. 10 repeals the licence requirement "Section 1 of this chapter does not apply to" and Sec. 9 replaces it with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun", so an adult not on that list may carry a handgun with no licence. That is a law that repeals the permit to carry (rung 5: "Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry"). Single-subject (season 3 verdict), ungated. His Yea on HB 1084 (2024), a capitol carry right for state officials, is out of scope since the 2026-11-12 ruling (not a rung act). His 2022 press-release words on a related bill (permitless carry) agree but are out of the current cycle and not relied on; the HB 1296 co-sponsorship is evidence of the bill as filed and is not cited.$r4$),
  ('250a7ae0-f130-449e-9625-4c2d1512bbf6', 5,
   $r4$Yea in the Senate on the HB 1296 (2022) conference committee report (the rung 5 act, runner ruling): Sec. 10 repeals the licence requirement "Section 1 of this chapter does not apply to" and Sec. 9 replaces it with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun", so an adult not on that list may carry a handgun with no licence. That is a law that repeals the permit to carry (rung 5: "Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry"). Single-subject (season 3 verdict), ungated. Her Senate Yea on HB 1084 (2024) (rung 4) sits below it.$r4$,
