  ('2f768304-a6f6-4b5a-b41d-000727f225a1', 5,
   $r4$Co-sponsor of IN HB 1296 (2022) and Yea on its House conference report, 2022-03-08. HB 1296 (2022) repeals the licence offence ("section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)") and lists who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun"; it removes the permit to carry for adults, which is rung 5 ("Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry"). Its list of persons barred from permit-free carry is the condition that the permit-removal law sets on its own permit-free carry, part of the rung 5 act (annex closure C3), not a separate rung 3 act. Single-subject verdict (season 3, codebook 0.6), census gate none. She also voted Yea on HB 1084 (2024), a rung 4 act; furthest act is 5. Her No on HB 1365 states no clear rung act, and her other ungated votes and co-sponsorships (HB 1235, HB 1323, HB 1274) are adjacent or direction-only. No restriction-side rung act of hers is ungated.$r4$,
