  ('375d5ba4-ab2a-4f1c-9d66-8c2349f517bc', 4,
   $r4$Every counted loosening act keeps the permit and makes carrying easier: HB 4030 (2021) cuts the CPL application fee from $100.00 to "not more than $45.00" (a lower fee: rung 4); HB 4284 (2025) cuts the concealed pistol licence renewal fee from $115.00 to "$30.00" (a lower fee, annex rule two: rung 4); HB 4855 (2025) lets an individual carry a loaded pistol while "hunting game with a bow and arrow" (carry allowed where it was barred, permit system kept: rung 4) (Yea and co-sponsor); HB 4980 (2025) lets an applicant apply to a county clerk in any county in this state instead of the county of residence (applying at a nearer office, annex rule two: rung 4) (Yea and co-sponsor); HB 5113 (2025) lets a CPL applicant resubmit a corrected application "without paying an additional fee" (an easier permit, a fee waiver, annex rule two: rung 4); HB 5187 (2021) bars an emergency order from acting to "Prohibit, regulate, or curtail the otherwise lawful possession, carrying" of a firearm (lifting a carry ban during a declared emergency: rung 4); SB 11 (2021) keeps county clerks' duty to issue concealed pistol licences during a declared emergency (permit kept, easier to get: rung 4). His No votes on the 2023 restrictions show a direction only; his prime sponsorship of HB 4434 (expired-CPL penalty) is adjacent; his campaign-site Second Amendment line names no policy. SB 22 (2023, airport sterile areas) restates a ban federal law already has and is read as no rung act; if it were read as a rung 3 place ban this record would turn two-sided, so this reading is flagged for the runner. Seats rung 4, "Make carrying a gun easier".$r4$,
