  ('598ae6bf-4b73-4106-bbf4-7323afa18ffa', 3,
   $r4$In his first term, quoted by WKZO (2025-06-04) on his bills to ban home-made guns with no serial numbers, he said: 'No one has any legitimate need for a ghost gun' … 'These dangerous weapons can't be traced by law enforcement. Why would we ever allow someone to have a weapon that can't be traced if used in a crime?' Not allowing anyone to have an untraceable, unserialised gun is a ban on having unserialised guns, a rung 3 act under annex rule one: 'Add limits on buying, having or carrying a gun' (serial numbers required, unserialised guns banned). His Yea on HB 5113 (CPL fee waiver after an error, rung 4) keeps the permit and, under the licence rule, does not conflict with a serial-number rule, so the record sits at rung 3. His Nays on HB 4284, HB 4855 and HB 4980 show a side only; HB 4478/4479 have no instrument file and are not cited as records.$r4$,
   $r4$In his first term, quoted by WKZO (2025-06-04) on his bills to ban home-made guns with no serial numbers, he said: 'No one has any legitimate need for a ghost gun' … 'These dangerous weapons can't be traced by law enforcement. Why would we ever allow someone to have a weapon that can't be traced if used in a crime?' Not allowing anyone to have an untraceable, unserialised gun is a ban on having unserialised guns, a rung 3 act under annex rule one: 'Add limits on buying, having or carrying a gun' (serial numbers required, unserialised guns banned). His Yea on HB 5113 (a free re-application after an error), which since the 2026-11-12 ruling shows only which side he is on and is not a rung act, conflicts with nothing, so the record sits at rung 3. His Nays on HB 4284, HB 4855 and HB 4980 show a side only; HB 4478/4479 have no instrument file and are not cited as records.$r4$),
