  ('64652750-ddd9-434f-b869-e95290d9eea4', 5,
   $r4$Yea on the House conference report of HB 1296 (2022) (2022-03-08, 68-30, gate none; the conference-report vote is the rung 5 act, runner ruling). Its text refers to "section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)", keeps only "a five (5) year or lifetime license to carry a handgun issued by the superintendent before July 1, 2022" valid, and replaces the licence with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun" (part of the permit-free carry rule, as closure C3, not a rung 3 act). Single-subject (season 3 verdict). That meets the rung "Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry". His Yea on the HB 1084 (2024) conference report (2024-03-06, 66-26, single-subject) says "A state officer who is not prohibited from possessing a handgun under state or federal law has the right to carry a handgun within the state capitol building" (rung 4, same side, below the furthest act). No restriction-side rung act is on his record: his Nay on HB 1365 (2023) is no rung act (IN ruling); SB 119 (2019) copies a federal ban and is near-unanimous; his other ungated Yeas (HB-1143-2024, HB-1235-2024, HB-1323-2023, HB-1274-2026, SB-176-2026) state no rung act; the rest are gated (multi-subject or near-unanimous). His HB-1296-2022 co-sponsorship is the bill as filed and is not relied on (IN ruling).$r4$,
