  ('65472fdd-f8b6-4a9c-8bfd-ae5c8e38af5e', 4,
   $r4$Yea on HB 4284 (2025), the concealed pistol licence renewal fee cut from "$115.00" to "$30.00", Yea and co-sponsor on HB 4980 (2025), an applicant may apply to a county clerk in any county in this state and HB 4855 (2025), the act does not prohibit an individual from transporting a pistol or carrying a loaded pistol, whether concealed or not, if any of the following apply: … "The individual is hunting game with a bow and arrow", Yea on HB 5113 (2025), after an application error the applicant "may submit a new application" … "without paying an additional fee": an easier carry permit and a wider class of carriers, rung 4 (annex rule two), with the permit kept. Single-subject bills on split House votes. He voted No on the rung 3 bills (HB 4138, 4146, SB 83, HB 4127, 4128), which shows a side only, and no record repeals a permit: rung 4, make carrying a gun easier. His sponsorships of HB 5381, 5377, 5132, 4285 and 4756 have no instrument file in the store and are not used; HB 4481 is gated near-unanimous. SB 22 (2023, weapons of every kind in an airport sterile area) is read as no rung act: it copies the federal sterile-area weapons ban, and its title says it clarifies an existing ban.$r4$,
