  ('9e2a7aa6-bc33-4c2d-91bb-71f766d49a2e', 5,
   $r4$Yea on IN HB 1296 (2022), single-subject, conference report 68-30 House / 30-20 Senate: it repeals the licence to carry (the text cites "section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)" and repeals IC 35-47-2-2), replacing it with a list of persons who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun"; that list is the permit-free carry rule's own eligibility line, part of the rung 5 act (annex closure C3): rung 5 "Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry". Yeas on IN HB 1084 (2024), single-subject, 66-26 House conference report (39-9 Senate): "A state officer who is not prohibited from possessing a handgun under state or federal law has the right to carry a handgun within the state capitol building and on the property of the state capitol complex.", on IN HB 1071 (2017), single-subject, conference report 74-26 House / 38-12 Senate: "A person may carry a handgun without a license if the person: (1) has applied for a license" … "(2) is protected by a protection order" for sixty days (a licence exemption for one group; the licence system stays, so rung 4 under the runner ruling on limited permit repeals) and on IN SB 43 (2017), single-subject, 76-16 House / Senate concurrence 39-7: "A member of the general assembly who: (1) possesses a valid Indiana license to carry a handgun" … "has the right to carry a handgun within the state capitol building" are rung 4 acts on the same side; furthest act gives 5. No rung act on the restriction side. Other gun findings are gated (near-unanimous or multi-subject) or out of scope (adjacent: shooting-range zoning SB 176, insurer gun-free-zone signs HB 1274, licence-holder privacy HB 1323, local suits against the industry HB 1235, police gun trades HB 1143); a vote on HB 1365 (2023, machine guns) is treated as no rung act (orchestrator note, runner ruling pending): it neither seats nor makes the record two-sided. If HB 1365 (2023) were read as a rung 2 act (its machine-gun definition), this person's ungated Yea on it would sit beside the rung 5 act on the other side of the middle, and the code would change to doesnt-fit (two-sided).$r4$,
