  ('a9bf758c-e902-40cc-ace0-b306c63eb936', 5,
   $r4$Co-sponsor of IN HB 1296 (2022) (LegiScan sponsor list) and Yea on its House conference report, 2022-03-08, 68-30. HB 1296 (2022) repeals the licence offence ("section 1 of this chapter (carrying a handgun without a license) (before its repeal)") and lists who "may not knowingly or intentionally carry a handgun"; it removes the permit to carry for adults, which is rung 5 ("Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry"). Its list of persons barred from permit-free carry is the condition that the permit-removal law sets on its own permit-free carry, part of the rung 5 act (annex closure C3), not a separate rung 3 act. Single-subject verdict (season 3, codebook 0.6), census gate none. He also voted Yea on HB 1084 (2024) and SB 43 (2017), both rung 4 carry-widening acts on the same side; furthest act is 5. No restriction-side rung act of his is ungated (HB 1651 and HB 1095 are near-unanimous; SB 335 and SB 158 multi-subject). His quote on the crime guns task force is adjacent. A Yea on HB 1365 (2023, machine guns) is treated as no rung act (orchestrator note); if it were read as rung 2, this record would become two-sided and the row a BLANK adjacent-chairs.$r4$,
