   $r4$Yea on the rung 3 acts HB 4138 (2023, 56-53: no one may "Purchase a firearm that is not a pistol in this state without first having obtained a license"); SB 83 (2023, 56-51: "the court shall issue an extreme risk protection order" on the stated finding); HB 4146 (2023, 56-52: a buyer qualifies only if "not subject to an extreme risk protection order"), and on the place bans HB 4127 (2023, 56-53: no one may "possess a firearm in a polling place or within 100 feet from any entrance"); HB 4128 (2024, 56-53: no one may "possess a firearm in an absent voter counting place" while ballots are processed). Yea also on the rung 4 act HB 4855 (2026, 90-13: carrying a loaded pistol is allowed when "The individual is hunting game with a bow and arrow"), each keeping the permit. Under the licence rule as ruled 2026-11-05 (runner, Michigan), a place ban and a permit-keeping easing do not conflict, and the rung 4 acts sit beside the rung 3 acts that limit who may buy or keep a gun (annex the licence rule); the record sits at rung 3, "Add limits on buying, having or carrying a gun, such as checking every buyer, red-flag orders, waiting periods or bans on guns in hospitals". It has no Yea on a type ban or a permit repeal. She co-sponsored HB 4146. Her Nays on other carry bills (HB 4003, HB 4030, HB 4284, HB 4434, HB 4980, HB 5113, HB 5187, SB 11) show a side only; SB 22 and SB 471 copy federal bans; HB 4481 is gated.$r4$,
