  ('b9e831c7-217d-4011-b069-d590a18f400a', 4,
   $r4$As State Representative she voted Yea on MI HB 4855 (2026-02-05, 90-13, gate none), allowing "carrying a loaded pistol, whether concealed or not" while "hunting game with a bow and arrow"; HB 4980 (2026-01-21, 60-45; a CPL applicant may apply to a county clerk in any county in this state); HB 4284 (2026-01-14, 63-46; CPL renewal fee "$115.00" to "$30.00"); and HB 5113 (reapply "without paying an additional fee"). Each keeps the permit and widens carry or makes the permit easier: 'Make carrying a gun easier, such as honoring carry permits from other states' (rung 4; annex rule two). No act repeals a permit and none is a rung 1-3 act. HB 4481 is gated (92-9); HB 4949 is adjacent. The search found no own words.$r4$,
