   $r4$Prime sponsor and Yea on HB 4855 (2025) lets an individual carry a loaded pistol while "hunting game with a bow and arrow" (carry allowed where it was barred, permit system kept: rung 4); also HB 4284 (2025) cuts the concealed pistol licence renewal fee from $115.00 to "$30.00" (a lower fee, annex rule two: rung 4); HB 4980 (2025) lets an applicant apply to a county clerk in any county in this state instead of the county of residence (applying at a nearer office, annex rule two: rung 4) (Yea and co-sponsor); HB 5113 (2025) lets a CPL applicant resubmit a corrected application "without paying an additional fee" (an easier permit, a fee waiver, annex rule two: rung 4); and co-sponsorship of HB 4943 (2023) bars the Capitol Commission from any rule to prevent "An individual licensed by this state or another state to carry a concealed pistol" from carrying in the Capitol (carry in more places for licence holders: rung 4; no floor vote on file, so the sponsorship is not gated). All keep the permit and make carrying easier (rung 4). His No votes and 2023 words against checks on every purchase ("Requiring a background check on every single firearm purchase is impractical") show a direction only (Q2). HB 4481 is gated. SB 22 (2023, airport sterile areas) restates a ban federal law already has and is read as no rung act; if it were read as a rung 3 place ban this record would turn two-sided, so this reading is flagged for the runner. Seats rung 4, "Make carrying a gun easier".$r4$,
